.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt ICMP6 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm icmp6
.Nd ICMPv6, IPv6's control messages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.In netinet/in.h
.In netinet/icmp6.h
.Ft int
.Fn socket "AF_INET6" "SOCK_RAW" "IPPROTO_ICMPV6"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
ICMPv6, RFC 4443, carries IPv6's errors, its echo requests and replies,
neighbour discovery and MLD
.Pq Xr ipv6 7 .
The kernel checks each message's checksum over the pseudo-header and
drops one that fails.
.Pp
It answers an echo request from the address it was sent to, or, sent to
a group, from its own address on the link it came by, with the request's
identifier, sequence and data, up to 65527 bytes, in fragments past the
path MTU.
An echo reply goes to the kernel's own ping
.Pq Xr ping 2 ,
which
.Xr ping 1
uses for an IPv6 address.
A Packet Too Big that quotes a datagram this machine sent lowers the path
MTU of its destination, never below 1280 bytes, for ten minutes.
A destination unreachable, a time exceeded or a parameter problem is
counted and given to the raw sockets alone.
Router and neighbour solicitations and advertisements are neighbour
discovery's, and MLD's queries and reports MLD's; a redirect is counted
and ignored.
.Pp
The errors the kernel sends are a port unreachable for a UDP datagram no
socket takes, an address unreachable for a datagram whose next hop never
answered, a parameter problem for a header it cannot take, and a time
exceeded for a reassembly not finished in 60 seconds.
None answers an error or a datagram to a group, but a parameter problem
about an unknown option whose type asks for one; each quotes as much of
the datagram as keeps it within 1280 bytes; and those to another host
leave at most one a second after a burst of six.
.Pp
A raw socket of
.Dv IPPROTO_ICMPV6 ,
which only effective user ID 0 may open, receives a copy of every ICMPv6
message the machine accepts, without its IPv6 header, and its sender, as
a
.Vt struct sockaddr_in6
whose scope id is the interface it came in on for a link-local sender.
A message sent on it goes with the checksum the kernel computes, under
the socket's IPv6 options, in fragments past the path MTU.
Its queue holds eight messages of up to 1500 bytes and drops the newest
when full.
Its
.Dv ICMP6_FILTER ,
at level
.Dv IPPROTO_ICMPV6 ,
blocks the types whose bits are set, before a message takes a place in
the queue; a new socket passes every type
.Pq Xr setsockopt 2 .
.Pp
.Pa /proc/net/snmp6
counts the messages received and sent, by type, and the malformed ones
.Pq Xr proc 5 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ping 1 ,
.Xr ping 2 ,
.Xr recv 2 ,
.Xr setsockopt 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr proc 5 ,
.Xr ipv6 7
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 4443, ICMPv6;
RFC 4861, neighbour discovery;
RFC 3810, MLDv2;
RFC 8201, path MTU discovery.
